    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0693" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/131: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Beaulac</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-03-15T14:00:00-05:45">March 15, 1932—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. Department’s 25, March 11, 6 p.m.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d650-f1"/>
                    Salvadorean delegates returned to San Salvador March 15. It is my understanding
                    that the President did not receive them and that they received no encouragement
                    in their mission. The Minister for Foreign Affairs has assured me that
                    Nicaragua’s policy with respect to Martínez has not changed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
